{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfweBxWckkDbibqB8EN6e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I didn't open the dashboard or check that the rule's query matches any documents.\n\n**Data:** The logs index has a `timestamp` time field and `response` as a string field, with `.keyword` variants. Other fields I used are `bytes`, `extension` and `clientip`. Others include `geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `machine.os`, `host`, `url` and `referer`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-7b483140 Web logs overview\" has four panels:\n- Total requests (metric)\n- Requests over time (area)\n- Responses by status code (pie)\n- Average bytes by extension (bar)\n\nIt is at `http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-7b483140-web-logs-overview-7f00961d1ee9`.\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-7b483140 5xx spike\" (id `717efe43-ae49-4517-a66d-cb6e9a2d13fa`) is an Elasticsearch query rule. It checks every minute and fires when more than 10 documents in the last 5 minutes have a `response.keyword` matching `5[0-9][0-9]`. The rule was created disabled, so I enabled it afterwards. It has no actions attached, so it will record alerts but won't notify anyone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":163,"cache_read_input_tokens":20326,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":163},"output_tokens":441,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"502ffde8-3b28-46c7-a188-513ee6717c3b","timestamp":"2026-10-12T03:35:13.015Z","request_id":"req_011CfweBxJyLWrHW5Ybz96WZ"}
